WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.150
ROSA: 'What would happen if
you stopped trusting them.

2
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:04.750
'and started trusting me?'

3
00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:06.450
There's a group I run.

4
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:09.450
It's a couple of times a
week. We're meeting tonight.

5
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.450
Come.

6
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:13.100
You NUTTER!

7
00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.450
- Why do you do this?
- Because I am you.

8
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:18.450
I am the darkest part of you.

9
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:19.450
I am despair.

10
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:21.100
I am death.

11
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.450
I'm just trying to find out the truth.

12
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:29.450
I'm trying to find out
who did this to you.

13
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:32.450
She was investigating something.

14
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:34.450
You have to tell Chrissie.

15
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:35.450
MICHAEL: I know him.

16
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:37.450
The man on your appeal.

17
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:41.450
He came in about three
months ago looking for a job.

18
00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.450
CHRISSIE: 12.5% of the population
within a few square miles.

19
00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:47.450
No wonder we can't find him.

20
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:49.450
One of the great invisibles.

21
00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:52.450
KHAALID: You have to find him.
Someone is going to kill him.

22
00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:54.450
HAIDER: We're born alone. we die alone.

23
00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:56.450
Only through love and
friendship can we create

24
00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:59.450
the illusion for the moment.
that we are not alone.

25
00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:02.450
CHRISSIE: We'll find who did this.

26
00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:05.170
Otherwise what are we good for?

27
00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:07.450
Can you see me yet?

28
00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.170
Night-night.

29
00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:13.500
I'm a state authorised judge. Go on.

30
00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:16.450
So? I had a second phone.

31
00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:19.450
MARCUS: Any headway on
the pay-as-you-go number

32
00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:22.170
found on Stevie's second phone?

33
00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:07.450
HAIDER: We come to this
country so filled with hope.

34
00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:10.450
so grateful for the potential.

35
00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:13.450
Yet still they say. "Why do
we leave our door blindly open

36
00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:15.450
"to these people?"

37
00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:17.900
But you migrated here too.

38
00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:22.440
You see what people here do not see.

39
00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:25.500
You of all people.

40
00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:30.000
If only you had seen
me clearly as I see you.

41
00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:33.450
See the loneliness.

42
00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:35.450
The isolation.

43
00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:41.450
What it is like to be so far
from your country and family.

44
00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:44.440
What it is like to try and fit here.

45
00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:48.500
How hard it is just to be.

46
00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:56.570
Would you excuse me?

47
00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:03.500
INDISTINCT

48
00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:25.500
Why was Stevie calling you?

49
00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:33.450
Does Chrissie know?

50
00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:37.450
That you have a second phone or
that you spoke to Stevie on it

51
00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:40.500
in the weeks leading up to her death?

52
00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:44.500
- It didn't seem relevant.
- To who?

53
00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:48.450
She was asking my advice.

54
00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:50.450
She had a friend. he was here illegally.

55
00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:54.450
For Christ's sake. Tom. that "friend"
was all over a police appeal.

56
00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.450
Yes. but I didn't know his
name. She didn't tell me.

57
00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:58.450
I didn't make the link.

58
00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:00.450
She wanted to know his
chances of staying here.

59
00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:01.450
and I agreed they were pretty slim.

60
00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:03.450
But I told her.

61
00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:05.450
without the right paperwork...
And his lawyer was pretty good.

62
00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:09.450
I mean. as good as any of us
are. She was trying to help him.

63
00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:11.840
And what were YOU doing?

64
00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:15.900
Oh. OK.

65
00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:22.450
This is a cheap pay-as-you-go
phone. and I use it for work.

66
00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:25.500
and the occasional recreational activity.

67
00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:34.450
What do you want from me?

68
00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:36.840
You should tell Chrissie.

69
00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:40.450
I know I should tell
Chrissie if I wasn't a shit.

70
00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:42.450
But I'm a shit.

71
00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:45.450
Like a lot of other shits with
a wife who barely looks at me.

72
00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:47.450
Now. I'm serious.

73
00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:50.450
The thought of seeing me naked is
more than repellent to Chrissie.

74
00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:51.450
It's practically laughable.

75
00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:54.450
She'd rather sleep with the dog than
spend a night cooched up with me.

76
00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:56.450
And I am mortgaged up to the hilt.

77
00:04:56.500 --> 00:04:58.450
I've got four delinquent
and selfish children.

78
00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:01.450
You know what? Forgive me if I
didn't make the very obvious link

79
00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:02.450
over a couple of phone calls.

80
00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:04.500
Four!

81
00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:07.450
You spoke to Stevie four times.

82
00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:09.840
One was 19 minutes long.

83
00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:12.450
I presumed they were screwing.

84
00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:15.450
No. That's YOUR style. Tom.

85
00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:16.450
Talk to Chrissie.

86
00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:18.450
And say what?

87
00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:19.450
We'll need a statement.

88
00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:21.840
Talk to her before then.

89
00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:29.450
CHRISSIE: The murder
of Haider Jamail Abdi.

90
00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:32.450
DS Stevenson was involved with him... How?

91
00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:37.450
We've established that the blue
Mondeo used in DS Stevenson's murder

92
00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:39.450
was owned by Mr Jamal Abdi.

93
00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:43.450
but it was not in his possession
after October the 17th.

94
00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:46.450
Five days later. it was used in the
drive-by shooting of DS Stevenson.

95
00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:51.450
We know that he sometimes stayed at
her flat. and our increasing concern

96
00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:55.450
is that the murder of Haider Jamal
Abdi and DS Stevenson are linked.

97
00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:59.450
They knew one another. We've ruled
out any sort of relationship.

98
00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:01.450
but we do know that she was
investigating something

99
00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:05.450
and Mr Jamal Abdi may
have been helping her.

100
00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:09.450
Was it this investigation
that led to their deaths?

101
00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:11.450
Mr Jamal Abdi was clearly frightened

102
00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:14.450
in the hours leading up to his murder.

103
00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:17.450
So. was someone trying to frame him? Who?

104
00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:21.450
And how does this link to
either or both of their murders?

105
00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:24.450
Ira has been meticulously going through

106
00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:27.450
the CCTV footage from the library.

107
00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:29.450
- Perhaps you'd like to
bring us up to speed. - Yeah.

108
00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:30.450
This is a list of names.

109
00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:32.450
No amber alerts as of yet.

110
00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:34.450
Those we know who took out books that day

111
00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:37.450
and were in the library. I've
gone through most of the people.

112
00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:39.450
but there are one or
two not yet identified.

113
00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:43.500
And unfortunately there wasn't
a camera angled on the murder.

114
00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:47.570
Where have you been?

115
00:06:49.500 --> 00:06:51.450
Coffee with a friend.

116
00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:53.450
SHE LAUGHS

117
00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:54.450
You have no friends.

118
00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:56.450
Well. that's not strictly true.

119
00:06:56.500 --> 00:06:58.240
I don't count.

120
00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:03.500
Are you all right?

121
00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:05.970
I'm fine.

122
00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:11.450
You're keeping something from
me. Do not go behind my back.

123
00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:15.450
Hostel in Whitechapel. Came in on
the appeal. We're going down now.

124
00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:17.450
Haider had been staying there.

125
00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:19.450
He signed in on the
night of Stevie's murder.

126
00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:21.450
Eyewitnesses saw him on
the phone to his wife.

127
00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:23.450
Then reading in his
room till gone midnight.

128
00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:26.500
I take it all back --
appeals forever more.

129
00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:32.040
What the hell was she up to?

130
00:07:33.500 --> 00:07:36.240
And who was he so frightened of?

131
00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:43.500
Oh. Ira said you had a new
lead. the pay-as-you-go.

132
00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:46.450
It got up and went.

133
00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:48.450
SHE CHUCKLES

134
00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:50.900
And now he gives me jokes.

135
00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:54.500
River...

136
00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:57.640
Come to me first. OK?

137
00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:00.640
Boss is on the prowl.

138
00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:05.500
Oh. Stevie's laptop.

139
00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:08.450
It's on your desk.

140
00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:14.450
We've pulled everything out now
-- search history. e-mails.

141
00:08:14.500 --> 00:08:18.450
cleaned up the hard drive.
etc. but there's... photos

142
00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:21.500
and... stuff I don't want to wipe. so...

143
00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:25.450
.. can you work out what to do with it?

144
00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:27.450
MOBILE PHONE VIBRATES

145
00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:29.450
Hi.

146
00:08:29.500 --> 00:08:31.450
No. No. no. no. no.

147
00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:34.450
You do not get out of
dinner tonight. my love.

148
00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:38.450
They... Tom! Listen to
me. they are your parents.

149
00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:40.040
SHE LAUGHS

150
00:08:56.500 --> 00:09:00.450
It's Stevie's search history.
I've trawled through it twice now.

151
00:09:00.500 --> 00:09:03.450
There's some repeated
searches. but no links yet.

152
00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:05.700
I'll go over it later.

153
00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:09.450
Cleaner. We're trying to trace him.

154
00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:12.450
He's there mopping the floor.
Library have no record of him.

155
00:09:12.500 --> 00:09:15.450
I'm pulling up what I can. but
most of the people there that day

156
00:09:15.500 --> 00:09:18.450
probably didn't even have a library card.

157
00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:22.500
Just skimming the free newspapers
and getting in from the cold.

158
00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:31.450
Haider's reading list --
the odd bit of poetry.

159
00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:33.450
a taste for Dan Brown novels.

160
00:09:33.500 --> 00:09:34.450
He'd checked out a couple of books

161
00:09:34.500 --> 00:09:37.450
on British citizenship
and the legal system.

162
00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:40.500
Why does everybody want
to come to this city?

163
00:09:41.500 --> 00:09:43.450
You did.

164
00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:45.450
I came because I had to. when I was 14.

165
00:09:45.500 --> 00:09:49.450
My grandmother died and
my mother lived here.

166
00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:52.450
First week. I lived on
peanut butter sandwiches.

167
00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:55.450
It was all she had in the
fridge. It rained all the time

168
00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:57.450
and nothing was green.

169
00:09:57.500 --> 00:09:59.640
I hated it. Hated it.

170
00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:02.450
But you stayed.

171
00:10:02.500 --> 00:10:04.700
It had its advantages.

172
00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:08.500
It's a city for everyone who
belongs to everywhere else.

173
00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:16.500
I went to Cork when I was 14.

174
00:10:20.500 --> 00:10:22.500
Rained there too.

175
00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:45.500
GUNSHOT

176
00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:50.500
HE PANTS

177
00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:11.500
PANICKY BREATHING

178
00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:16.840
River!

179
00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:21.040
All right?

180
00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:31.770
Yeah.

181
00:11:43.500 --> 00:11:45.500
I can drive.

182
00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:52.500
It's fine.

183
00:12:00.500 --> 00:12:02.500
She's gone.

184
00:12:04.500 --> 00:12:06.500
How would you know?

185
00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:12.450
I'm getting a feel for it.

186
00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:13.450
Right...

187
00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:15.500
HE CHUCKLES

188
00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:19.840
Right.

189
00:12:21.500 --> 00:12:23.500
Right.

190
00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:59.500
CHATTER

191
00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:17.500
Excuse me. is it all right if you
just pull out some records for us?

192
00:13:22.500 --> 00:13:24.500
CHATTER

193
00:13:36.450 --> 00:13:37.450
Haider had been here nearly three months.

194
00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:39.450
and moved out the day after Stevie died.

195
00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:42.450
That must have been when
he moved in with Khaalid.

196
00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:44.450
They said it's worth talking to...

197
00:13:44.500 --> 00:13:47.450
to Mrs Sunday Akentola. She's
the hostel's immigration lawyer.

198
00:13:47.500 --> 00:13:50.450
She comes in twice a week and Haider
had a couple of meetings with her.

199
00:13:50.500 --> 00:13:53.450
Most likely to get the process
started. but no-one knows

200
00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:54.450
if he followed through.

201
00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:56.450
Mrs Akentola.

202
00:13:56.500 --> 00:13:58.450
Sorry... Sorry. I've
finished up for today.

203
00:13:58.500 --> 00:14:01.450
It's all right. the last
thing we need is a lawyer.

204
00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:04.450
Do you mind if we walk?

205
00:14:04.500 --> 00:14:07.450
I've got an appointment
back in my office in...

206
00:14:07.500 --> 00:14:08.970
oh. now.

207
00:14:11.500 --> 00:14:16.500
Paperwork. June. for a Mr Haider
Jamal Abdi. Please. do sit.

208
00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:24.450
- Here you are. Sunday.
- Thanks. June. A very nice man.

209
00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:28.450
I am sorry I didn't make the
association in the press.

210
00:14:28.500 --> 00:14:31.100
Have you ever seen this woman?

211
00:14:32.500 --> 00:14:33.640
No.

212
00:14:34.500 --> 00:14:36.700
So he came on his own?

213
00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:39.450
Yes. Yes. Always on his own.

214
00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:42.450
His wife was in...

215
00:14:42.500 --> 00:14:45.500
Mogadishu. Yes. Very smart. Very nice man.

216
00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:49.500
Very sad.

217
00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:54.970
Do you have more paperwork?

218
00:14:55.500 --> 00:14:57.450
Er. yes... Yes.

219
00:14:57.500 --> 00:15:01.450
The problem is. everyone says we make it

220
00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:04.450
so easy for these people to come in.

221
00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:07.450
but the Home Office
lawyers. they are vicious.

222
00:15:07.500 --> 00:15:12.450
All are guilty until proven
innocent in a system that is broken.

223
00:15:12.500 --> 00:15:15.440
It's not what you can become here...

224
00:15:15.500 --> 00:15:18.450
.. it's what you are.

225
00:15:18.500 --> 00:15:21.450
And we wonder why they
come in underground.

226
00:15:21.500 --> 00:15:26.450
Illegally. My job is to legitimise them.

227
00:15:26.500 --> 00:15:28.450
Do you have a client list?

228
00:15:28.500 --> 00:15:30.500
Yes.

229
00:15:31.500 --> 00:15:33.450
WOMAN: I'm heading over to the
hostel now. then back to court.

230
00:15:33.500 --> 00:15:35.450
Thanks. Ema.

231
00:15:35.500 --> 00:15:37.240
Client list...

232
00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:44.450
I saw you at the
immigration court earlier.

233
00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:46.450
Yes. yeah...

234
00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:47.450
You work there?

235
00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:50.450
I work for a few clients. Legal
firms. wherever I am needed.

236
00:15:50.500 --> 00:15:52.970
Have you ever met this man?

237
00:15:54.500 --> 00:15:56.450
He was staying at the hostel.

238
00:15:56.500 --> 00:15:59.450
I'm sorry. I don't speak Arabic.

239
00:15:59.500 --> 00:16:02.450
Um. his name. he's... he's Arabic. no?

240
00:16:02.500 --> 00:16:05.500
No. Somalian. He was a client here.

241
00:16:06.500 --> 00:16:08.450
I speak French. Romanian. Russian.

242
00:16:08.500 --> 00:16:10.450
a bit of Italian -- badly.

243
00:16:10.500 --> 00:16:13.440
Did you ever see this woman before?

244
00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:18.700
I saw her on the news.

245
00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:23.370
Yes. she came in a few months ago.

246
00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:25.770
Together with this man?

247
00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:28.450
Maybe.

248
00:16:28.500 --> 00:16:30.450
Maybe. yes.

249
00:16:30.500 --> 00:16:32.700
Yes. maybe it WAS him.

250
00:16:34.500 --> 00:16:37.450
She came in with him once or twice.

251
00:16:37.500 --> 00:16:40.450
And then she came back alone. Once.

252
00:16:40.500 --> 00:16:43.600
Mrs Akentola said she'd never met her.

253
00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:47.450
Then I'm wrong. I'm sorry.
Today is the worst day.

254
00:16:47.500 --> 00:16:51.450
Friday is court day. so
we're building up to that.

255
00:16:51.500 --> 00:16:54.450
I need to get back there. back
and forth. back and forth...

256
00:16:54.500 --> 00:16:56.450
Are you sure you're wrong?

257
00:16:56.500 --> 00:17:01.450
We suspect she was investigating
something and this may be it.

258
00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:03.370
You can help us.

259
00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:08.450
Please don't say I told you.

260
00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:10.240
She knows her.

261
00:17:11.500 --> 00:17:13.700
Mrs Akentola knew her.

262
00:17:25.500 --> 00:17:28.450
My suspicion is this is only a
fraction of her client list.

263
00:17:28.500 --> 00:17:31.450
but she has a pretty good
strike rate. Mrs Akentola.

264
00:17:31.500 --> 00:17:34.500
Then why is she lying
about meeting Stevie?

265
00:17:36.500 --> 00:17:39.900
If you're covering up
an immigration scam...

266
00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:41.450
That's what she was investigating.

267
00:17:41.500 --> 00:17:43.500
Exactly. my friend.

268
00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:49.500
There's nothing here. Overstayed
visa. odd asylum case.

269
00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:54.450
What's interesting is...
Most of them go to appeal.

270
00:17:54.500 --> 00:17:57.500
and only on appeal do
they get a right to stay.

271
00:18:02.500 --> 00:18:04.100
Mayonnaise.

272
00:18:05.450 --> 00:18:06.450
Big mistake.

273
00:18:06.500 --> 00:18:08.500
Four points.

274
00:18:12.450 --> 00:18:13.450
It's not late.

275
00:18:13.500 --> 00:18:15.450
- I'm here.
- What?

276
00:18:15.500 --> 00:18:17.450
- I'm sitting right opposite.
- Yeah.

277
00:18:17.500 --> 00:18:22.500
So you could talk. You could
talk to me instead of her.

278
00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:25.450
I could.

279
00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:29.900
But then you'd have to have
something interesting to say.

280
00:18:32.500 --> 00:18:33.970
HE SIGHS

281
00:18:35.500 --> 00:18:38.500
- Found something?
- Maybe. I'm not sure yet.

282
00:18:42.500 --> 00:18:44.450
River?

283
00:18:44.500 --> 00:18:46.450
Are you free tonight?

284
00:18:46.500 --> 00:18:47.450
My wife's cooking dinner

285
00:18:47.500 --> 00:18:49.450
and said...

286
00:18:49.500 --> 00:18:52.450
She said I should ask you
if you'd like to come over.

287
00:18:52.500 --> 00:18:54.450
I'm busy.

288
00:18:54.500 --> 00:18:56.450
Sure.

289
00:18:56.500 --> 00:18:58.450
Sure. Another time.

290
00:18:58.500 --> 00:18:59.450
Um... What is she cooking?

291
00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:01.450
Probably something... meat...

292
00:19:01.500 --> 00:19:04.500
There'll probably be
some meat of some kind.

293
00:19:05.500 --> 00:19:07.500
Lamb. maybe.

294
00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:10.450
I don't like lamb.

295
00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:12.500
There you go.

296
00:19:17.500 --> 00:19:20.500
MUFFLED ARGUING

297
00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:31.450
I'm going nowhere.

298
00:19:31.500 --> 00:19:33.450
Oh. River.

299
00:19:33.500 --> 00:19:35.040
You go on.

300
00:19:38.500 --> 00:19:40.900
We're in filling in forms.

301
00:19:42.500 --> 00:19:45.450
I'm trying to keep them calm. but
it's all storm with that family.

302
00:19:45.500 --> 00:19:46.450
What forms?

303
00:19:46.500 --> 00:19:49.450
Compensation. They've
taken advice. apparently.

304
00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:53.450
This is where Stevie would have come
in. you know. acted as my ballast.

305
00:19:53.500 --> 00:19:55.450
Do you want me to talk to them?

306
00:19:55.500 --> 00:19:58.450
No. no. You've got enough on your plate.

307
00:19:58.500 --> 00:20:01.500
Um. are we... getting any closer?

308
00:20:03.500 --> 00:20:05.450
I'll take that as a hopeful sign.

309
00:20:05.500 --> 00:20:07.500
THEY CHUCKLE

310
00:20:18.500 --> 00:20:21.500
That family... Vultures.

311
00:20:23.500 --> 00:20:25.450
They're grieving.

312
00:20:25.500 --> 00:20:28.450
The press don't help. Six weeks.

313
00:20:28.500 --> 00:20:30.450
For Christ's sake. six weeks.

314
00:20:30.500 --> 00:20:33.500
- You can't let them dictate.
- Yeah.

315
00:20:34.500 --> 00:20:36.570
So. er. Rosa's sick.

316
00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:39.450
Right.

317
00:20:39.500 --> 00:20:41.450
We were meant to go out last night.

318
00:20:41.500 --> 00:20:43.450
but she seems fine today.

319
00:20:43.500 --> 00:20:44.450
CHRISSIE: Tom. listen to me.

320
00:20:44.500 --> 00:20:45.450
Do you think she seems fine?

321
00:20:45.500 --> 00:20:48.450
- They are your parents. >
- Good. Good.

322
00:20:48.500 --> 00:20:50.450
And you need to start taking
responsibility. do you hear me?

323
00:20:50.500 --> 00:20:53.500
Sorry. Sorry! Keep me posted.

324
00:20:56.500 --> 00:20:59.450
- Marcus and Rosa. are they...?
- Are you following me?

325
00:20:59.500 --> 00:21:00.450
This is the men's.

326
00:21:00.500 --> 00:21:02.450
But...

327
00:21:02.500 --> 00:21:05.450
If I was having a pee. would
you hover outside like that?

328
00:21:05.500 --> 00:21:06.450
Yeah.

329
00:21:06.500 --> 00:21:08.450
Are they?

330
00:21:08.500 --> 00:21:09.450
No.

331
00:21:09.500 --> 00:21:11.450
I don't think so.

332
00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:13.450
He might want to. but...

333
00:21:13.500 --> 00:21:16.450
Did he say that? Oh. God.

334
00:21:16.500 --> 00:21:18.450
Of course.

335
00:21:18.500 --> 00:21:21.450
Why wouldn't a beautiful
30-something like Rosa

336
00:21:21.500 --> 00:21:26.450
go for a balding. self-opinionated
older man? I mean...

337
00:21:26.500 --> 00:21:28.450
Yeah. what a catch(!)

338
00:21:28.500 --> 00:21:31.450
God. the arrogance of you
men. To think that...

339
00:21:31.500 --> 00:21:33.450
Is that it?

340
00:21:33.500 --> 00:21:35.450
Have you finished?

341
00:21:35.500 --> 00:21:41.450
It doesn't matter that I am heading
up this entire investigation.

342
00:21:41.500 --> 00:21:45.450
It doesn't matter that he keeps
shoving me in front of the press.

343
00:21:45.500 --> 00:21:50.450
The weekly humiliation
of questions unanswered.

344
00:21:50.500 --> 00:21:52.450
Can you...?

345
00:21:52.500 --> 00:21:53.970
SHE SIGHS

346
00:21:55.500 --> 00:21:58.450
What do I say. River?

347
00:21:58.500 --> 00:22:01.450
We have nothing. Nothing! Marcus is right.

348
00:22:01.500 --> 00:22:03.500
Six weeks.

349
00:22:04.500 --> 00:22:06.450
Tom has cancelled...

350
00:22:06.500 --> 00:22:10.450
So now I have to cook and smile

351
00:22:10.500 --> 00:22:13.450
and sing Happy-sodding-Birthday

352
00:22:13.500 --> 00:22:16.450
to a man who has neither the
inclination nor the teeth

353
00:22:16.500 --> 00:22:19.450
to even eat sodding birthday cake.

354
00:22:19.500 --> 00:22:23.450
Which I also made. Whilst
doing this job. While he...

355
00:22:23.500 --> 00:22:25.450
he...

356
00:22:25.500 --> 00:22:27.450
If people say they have
to work late. do they?

357
00:22:27.500 --> 00:22:29.900
Do they have to work late?

358
00:22:31.500 --> 00:22:34.100
Is he having an affair... Tom?

359
00:22:36.500 --> 00:22:38.840
What makes you say that?

360
00:22:39.500 --> 00:22:41.300
Do I even care?

361
00:22:42.500 --> 00:22:45.450
All these bloody women with
their ridiculous names.

362
00:22:45.500 --> 00:22:47.450
Pretty...

363
00:22:47.500 --> 00:22:49.240
and clever...

364
00:22:50.500 --> 00:22:52.240
.. and young.

365
00:22:54.500 --> 00:22:56.450
He introduces them to me.

366
00:22:56.500 --> 00:22:58.450
I surprised him last week.

367
00:22:58.500 --> 00:23:02.450
He was embracing this tiny.
tiny. little elfin thing.

368
00:23:02.500 --> 00:23:04.450
with a pink woolly hat and...

369
00:23:04.500 --> 00:23:06.500
so pretty.

370
00:23:07.500 --> 00:23:09.450
Then he kissed me in front of her

371
00:23:09.500 --> 00:23:13.500
and whisked me off before
I could make a scene.

372
00:23:15.500 --> 00:23:18.450
Apparently she was terribly upset
because her hours had been cut

373
00:23:18.500 --> 00:23:21.450
and apparently it's highly competitive

374
00:23:21.500 --> 00:23:24.040
for interpreters these days.

375
00:23:24.500 --> 00:23:26.450
I consoled him. [MIRTHLESS LAUGH]

376
00:23:26.500 --> 00:23:29.450
- He's an ass.
- Yeah. Yeah.

377
00:23:29.500 --> 00:23:32.450
That's what Stevie used to say.

378
00:23:32.500 --> 00:23:33.900
Ohhh...

379
00:23:40.450 --> 00:23:41.450
She gave you that money. didn't she?

380
00:23:41.500 --> 00:23:44.450
That's what she was giving you
outside the restaurant. The 10K.

381
00:23:44.500 --> 00:23:46.500
I'm not an idiot.

382
00:23:47.500 --> 00:23:49.450
They were her total life savings

383
00:23:49.500 --> 00:23:53.450
and. in the event that anything
should happen. she had this idea

384
00:23:53.500 --> 00:23:56.500
that she'd give it to you because
you'd know what to do with it best.

385
00:23:57.500 --> 00:24:00.450
That's what she's giving you. isn't it?

386
00:24:00.500 --> 00:24:03.100
She knew something was coming.

387
00:24:04.500 --> 00:24:05.770
Yeah.

388
00:24:09.500 --> 00:24:12.450
I told you you were
keeping something from me.

389
00:24:12.500 --> 00:24:14.450
Her internet searches.

390
00:24:14.500 --> 00:24:17.440
I know we dismissed a lot of them...

391
00:24:17.500 --> 00:24:20.450
But the list of companies
she was researching.

392
00:24:20.500 --> 00:24:23.450
there are some interesting names
and there's a connection somewhere.

393
00:24:23.500 --> 00:24:25.100
So find it.

394
00:24:33.500 --> 00:24:35.570
Don't work too late.

395
00:25:26.500 --> 00:25:28.700
You know he's married?

396
00:25:33.500 --> 00:25:38.500
This is not out of some prurient
interest. but if it can help...

397
00:25:41.500 --> 00:25:44.500
Personally. I'm not a great
advocate for infidelity.

398
00:25:46.500 --> 00:25:49.450
Not that I have much experience. but...

399
00:25:49.500 --> 00:25:51.500
I imagine that...

400
00:25:53.500 --> 00:25:58.450
.. you never feel entirely
alone with the one you love.

401
00:25:58.500 --> 00:26:01.500
There will always be
another person in the room.

402
00:26:07.500 --> 00:26:09.640
And I can see you do.

403
00:26:13.500 --> 00:26:19.450
At this minute. Tom's wife is cooking
a birthday dinner for his father

404
00:26:19.500 --> 00:26:20.450
and his four children.

405
00:26:20.500 --> 00:26:26.450
And again. no judgment. but it
is a pretty shitty thing to do.

406
00:26:26.500 --> 00:26:29.450
His father. the old man.
is nearly 80 years old.

407
00:26:29.500 --> 00:26:32.440
Probably put him through law school.

408
00:26:33.500 --> 00:26:36.450
But he'd rather be spending
the night with his mistress.

409
00:26:36.500 --> 00:26:38.500
He's working late.

410
00:26:41.500 --> 00:26:43.640
He told you that too?

411
00:26:46.500 --> 00:26:49.450
DRY LAUGH

412
00:26:49.500 --> 00:26:51.170
The bastard.

413
00:26:56.500 --> 00:26:59.440
You need to tell me what's going on.

414
00:27:00.500 --> 00:27:03.450
I want Mrs Akentola's entire client list.

415
00:27:03.500 --> 00:27:07.450
Not just the sanitised
version that she's given me.

416
00:27:07.500 --> 00:27:09.450
As far as I can see.

417
00:27:09.500 --> 00:27:12.500
the cases that Mrs Akentola
runs through are pretty hopeless.

418
00:27:14.500 --> 00:27:17.600
So why do so many of them get through?

419
00:27:21.500 --> 00:27:23.840
I really need to go now.

420
00:27:26.500 --> 00:27:28.500
Bastard.

421
00:28:12.500 --> 00:28:14.500
Ah. Inspector.

422
00:28:15.500 --> 00:28:17.500
Ever closer.

423
00:28:18.500 --> 00:28:21.500
Yet ever further from the
truth of who she was.

424
00:28:25.500 --> 00:28:28.170
Don't you have somewhere to be?

425
00:28:39.500 --> 00:28:43.450
River... in a completely sane world.

426
00:28:43.500 --> 00:28:46.240
is madness not the only freedom?

427
00:28:46.500 --> 00:28:49.450
Why would one not take
oneself to the boundless edge

428
00:28:49.500 --> 00:28:52.370
when there is darkness all around?

429
00:28:53.500 --> 00:28:55.240
Give in to it.

430
00:28:56.500 --> 00:28:59.500
Give in to it as a child
does to his mother.

431
00:29:00.500 --> 00:29:02.450
Until. wilful...

432
00:29:02.500 --> 00:29:04.240
he defies her.

433
00:29:17.500 --> 00:29:22.450
MAN: So I grabbed him and I
said. "Listen. you muppet.

434
00:29:22.500 --> 00:29:27.450
"I've paid your shitty fare. now
drop me on the corner like I asked."

435
00:29:27.500 --> 00:29:30.450
And he's like. "The postcode you entered

436
00:29:30.500 --> 00:29:32.450
"is at the bottom of
the road." And I'm like.

437
00:29:32.500 --> 00:29:36.450
"I know where I live. shithead!"

438
00:29:36.500 --> 00:29:41.450
And then I see I'm in my own car.

439
00:29:41.500 --> 00:29:45.200
I'm driving up a one-way
street the wrong way...

440
00:29:45.500 --> 00:29:47.450
.. and it's the sat nav.

441
00:29:47.500 --> 00:29:50.450
I'm talking to that sat nav.

442
00:29:50.500 --> 00:29:51.450
That's the new voice.

443
00:29:51.500 --> 00:29:53.450
ANOTHER MAN CHUCKLES

444
00:29:53.500 --> 00:29:56.100
So I obey it all the way home.

445
00:29:57.500 --> 00:30:00.450
Took me three hours
round the North Circular.

446
00:30:00.500 --> 00:30:01.450
I only live ten minutes away.

447
00:30:01.500 --> 00:30:04.450
HE LAUGHS

448
00:30:04.500 --> 00:30:07.440
My girlfriend asked why I was late.

449
00:30:08.500 --> 00:30:11.450
I said I'd dropped off
for a drink at the pub.

450
00:30:11.500 --> 00:30:13.450
I couldn't tell her.

451
00:30:13.500 --> 00:30:16.100
"He's been a real shit today.

452
00:30:16.500 --> 00:30:19.450
"He's talking through the sat nav now."

453
00:30:19.500 --> 00:30:21.450
But I will.

454
00:30:21.500 --> 00:30:24.450
I will tell her.

455
00:30:24.500 --> 00:30:27.700
- Thanks. Thank you.
- Thank you. Robbie.

456
00:30:30.500 --> 00:30:34.450
If we are to see our voices
as articulating those emotions

457
00:30:34.500 --> 00:30:38.450
that perhaps we have hidden in
the remotest parts of ourselves.

458
00:30:38.500 --> 00:30:41.450
then I'd say that wasn't
bad. Robbie. for him.

459
00:30:41.500 --> 00:30:44.450
MAN CHUCKLES

460
00:30:44.500 --> 00:30:47.450
He was helping you that day.

461
00:30:47.500 --> 00:30:50.450
He wasn't telling you to throw
yourself under that train.

462
00:30:50.500 --> 00:30:51.640
OK.

463
00:30:53.500 --> 00:30:56.500
OK. Anyone else?

464
00:31:00.450 --> 00:31:01.450
River?

465
00:31:01.500 --> 00:31:04.450
This is your second session. Is
there anything you want to say?

466
00:31:04.500 --> 00:31:05.640
No.

467
00:31:06.500 --> 00:31:10.450
I know everyone would be very
supportive of your story.

468
00:31:10.500 --> 00:31:12.170
MAN CHUCKLES

469
00:31:13.500 --> 00:31:15.500
My story.

470
00:31:17.500 --> 00:31:20.450
You've listened to everyone else's.

471
00:31:20.500 --> 00:31:22.450
So. um...

472
00:31:22.500 --> 00:31:25.500
what have you thought. hearing
how other people are coping?

473
00:31:27.500 --> 00:31:29.500
What I've thought?

474
00:31:30.500 --> 00:31:31.700
Yes.

475
00:31:39.450 --> 00:31:40.450
Silence has a presence.

476
00:31:40.500 --> 00:31:42.500
HE LAUGHS

477
00:31:45.500 --> 00:31:49.500
Do you make that shit up yourself?
"Silence has a presence."

478
00:31:50.500 --> 00:31:52.500
What does it mean?

479
00:31:55.500 --> 00:31:58.300
Do you want to know what I think?

480
00:32:03.500 --> 00:32:06.450
I think our friend here should buy a map.

481
00:32:06.500 --> 00:32:10.450
Everyone drives with sat
nav now and yet nobody knows

482
00:32:10.500 --> 00:32:13.700
where they're going or how they got there.

483
00:32:14.450 --> 00:32:15.450
That would shut his voice up.

484
00:32:15.500 --> 00:32:17.450
I think that Twinkle-Toes.

485
00:32:17.500 --> 00:32:20.450
that your concern that you
haven't met a boyfriend

486
00:32:20.500 --> 00:32:23.450
because your voices
keep telling you not to

487
00:32:23.500 --> 00:32:26.440
is self delusion of the worst kind.

488
00:32:26.500 --> 00:32:29.450
Our baby here -- I have the
greatest sympathy for you.

489
00:32:29.500 --> 00:32:33.450
In this company. I'd be hanging
out with Kurt Cobain in my head.

490
00:32:33.500 --> 00:32:35.450
There are worse role models.

491
00:32:35.500 --> 00:32:38.450
although the drugs and
suicide aren't ideal.

492
00:32:38.500 --> 00:32:40.450
Your spots will go away.

493
00:32:40.500 --> 00:32:42.450
and I'd go as far as to say
that you're my favourite.

494
00:32:42.500 --> 00:32:45.450
Bar you. my friend. Bar you. my friend.

495
00:32:45.500 --> 00:32:46.450
MAN CHUCKLES

496
00:32:46.500 --> 00:32:48.970
I want to be where you are.

497
00:32:49.500 --> 00:32:53.450
You are clearly having a much
better time than this sorry group

498
00:32:53.500 --> 00:32:57.450
of self-absorbed. moaning.
infantilised freaks!

499
00:32:57.500 --> 00:33:00.450
Very good. Inspector. Very good.

500
00:33:00.500 --> 00:33:02.840
Laugh on and laugh loud!

501
00:33:03.500 --> 00:33:06.450
Because. frankly. this last...

502
00:33:06.500 --> 00:33:08.570
mind-numbing hour...

503
00:33:09.500 --> 00:33:11.450
.. is an hour I will never
get back in my life.

504
00:33:11.500 --> 00:33:14.040
Which brings me back to you.

505
00:33:15.500 --> 00:33:18.450
No children yet. How old are you?

506
00:33:18.500 --> 00:33:21.450
Fertility drops radically at 35.

507
00:33:21.500 --> 00:33:24.500
You might want to think about that.

508
00:33:25.500 --> 00:33:29.450
Whatever warped Messiah complex
you have might be better served

509
00:33:29.500 --> 00:33:32.450
directed towards those you love.

510
00:33:32.500 --> 00:33:34.450
than those you wouldn't even

511
00:33:34.500 --> 00:33:38.200
share a cup of coffee
with outside of this room.

512
00:33:38.500 --> 00:33:43.450
As Groucho Marx so famously said
"I refuse to join a club that...

513
00:33:43.500 --> 00:33:45.450
".. that would have me as a member.'

514
00:33:45.500 --> 00:33:47.450
CREAM AND RIVER LAUGH

515
00:33:47.500 --> 00:33:50.450
So consider this my
resignation. My cancellation.

516
00:33:50.500 --> 00:33:53.450
I don't need my two? £2 dues back.

517
00:33:53.500 --> 00:33:56.450
because the coffee was
better than the company.

518
00:33:56.500 --> 00:33:58.640
CREAM AND RIVER LAUGH

519
00:34:06.500 --> 00:34:09.500
So... that's something.

520
00:34:16.500 --> 00:34:17.840
Right.

521
00:34:19.500 --> 00:34:21.840
Sorry. have you finished?

522
00:34:29.500 --> 00:34:32.450
So let's remember that we don't
censor anyone's voices here.

523
00:34:32.500 --> 00:34:33.450
MAN CHUCKLES

524
00:34:33.500 --> 00:34:36.500
So. um... thank you. River.

525
00:34:37.500 --> 00:34:39.040
Thank you.

526
00:34:41.500 --> 00:34:43.450
OK. same time Thursday.

527
00:34:43.500 --> 00:34:45.570
Thank you. everyone.

528
00:34:48.500 --> 00:34:50.500
MAN CHUCKLES

529
00:34:53.500 --> 00:34:55.500
MAN CHUCKLES

530
00:35:27.500 --> 00:35:29.500
Don't let him in.

531
00:35:31.500 --> 00:35:33.570
He's coming for you.

532
00:35:46.500 --> 00:35:48.500
DISTANT CHANTING

533
00:35:49.500 --> 00:35:53.450
MEN CHANT: Who are ya? Who are ya?
Who are ya? Who are ya? Who are ya?

534
00:35:53.500 --> 00:35:55.500
CHANTING CONTINUES

535
00:35:59.500 --> 00:36:01.500
Who are ya?

536
00:36:06.450 --> 00:36:07.450
What the hell?!

537
00:36:07.500 --> 00:36:09.500
Crazy. man!

538
00:36:37.500 --> 00:36:39.500
River?

539
00:36:44.500 --> 00:36:46.500
It's all right.

540
00:36:49.500 --> 00:36:51.300
It's all right.

541
00:37:03.500 --> 00:37:06.450
♪ Sunny

542
00:37:06.500 --> 00:37:09.500
♪ Yesterday my life was filled with rain

543
00:37:11.500 --> 00:37:12.900
♪ Sunny

544
00:37:14.500 --> 00:37:18.450
♪ You smiled at me and
really eased the pain

545
00:37:18.500 --> 00:37:22.450
♪ Now the dark days are done
and the bright days are here

546
00:37:22.500 --> 00:37:27.450
♪ My Sunny one shines so sincere

547
00:37:27.500 --> 00:37:30.500
♪ Sunny one. so true. I love you

548
00:37:33.500 --> 00:37:35.500
♪ Sunny

549
00:37:36.500 --> 00:37:39.500
♪ Thank you for the sunshine bouquet

550
00:37:41.500 --> 00:37:42.900
♪ Sunny

551
00:37:43.500 --> 00:37:46.500
♪ Thank you for the love
you brought my way... ♪

552
00:37:50.500 --> 00:37:52.170
STEVIE: Red.

553
00:37:54.500 --> 00:37:56.040
No. white.

554
00:37:57.500 --> 00:37:59.450
Red.

555
00:37:59.500 --> 00:38:02.100
Stick with... Stick with red.

556
00:38:03.500 --> 00:38:04.900
♪ Sunny

557
00:38:06.500 --> 00:38:10.500
♪ Thank you for the truth you let me see

558
00:38:11.500 --> 00:38:13.450
♪ Sunny... ♪

559
00:38:13.500 --> 00:38:15.500
CORK POPS

560
00:38:16.500 --> 00:38:18.500
Breathe.

561
00:38:21.500 --> 00:38:24.240
What have you got in the fridge?

562
00:38:31.500 --> 00:38:33.450
Eggs.

563
00:38:33.500 --> 00:38:34.770
Good.

564
00:38:35.500 --> 00:38:38.450
- Now. remember how you do this.
- Yeah.

565
00:38:38.500 --> 00:38:41.500
- Because we went over this.
- Yeah.

566
00:38:42.500 --> 00:38:44.500
Pour the wine.

567
00:39:07.500 --> 00:39:09.900
Are you hungry? It's late.

568
00:39:16.500 --> 00:39:18.450
I-I could...

569
00:39:18.500 --> 00:39:20.450
I have eggs.

570
00:39:20.500 --> 00:39:22.450
Eggs is good.

571
00:39:22.500 --> 00:39:23.840
Right.

572
00:39:30.450 --> 00:39:31.450
You want more?

573
00:39:31.500 --> 00:39:33.500
No. No.

574
00:39:35.500 --> 00:39:37.450
Good eggs.

575
00:39:37.500 --> 00:39:39.100
HE CHUCKLES

576
00:39:42.500 --> 00:39:44.450
Do you cook a lot?

577
00:39:44.500 --> 00:39:45.450
Oh. when I can.

578
00:39:45.500 --> 00:39:47.640
MOBILE PHONE VIBRATES

579
00:39:51.500 --> 00:39:53.840
- Go ahead. you...
- No.

580
00:39:57.500 --> 00:39:59.500
SIREN WAILS

581
00:40:16.500 --> 00:40:18.450
Tonight...

582
00:40:18.500 --> 00:40:20.240
What I said...

583
00:40:20.500 --> 00:40:22.450
.. particularly about children...

584
00:40:22.500 --> 00:40:23.640
Oh.

585
00:40:30.500 --> 00:40:32.500
I did have a child.

586
00:40:36.500 --> 00:40:38.700
She died at six weeks.

587
00:40:39.450 --> 00:40:40.450
So...

588
00:40:40.500 --> 00:40:42.040
I'm sorry.

589
00:40:53.500 --> 00:40:56.500
And you should note that I've
shared coffee with you...

590
00:40:58.500 --> 00:41:00.300
.. what? Twice?

591
00:41:02.500 --> 00:41:04.500
And now eggs. so...

592
00:41:10.500 --> 00:41:13.450
'The number you have
called is unavailable.

593
00:41:13.500 --> 00:41:15.450
'Please leave a message after the tone.

594
00:41:15.500 --> 00:41:18.600
'or press one to change your message.'

595
00:41:53.500 --> 00:41:56.500
OVERLAPPING EXCITED VOICES

596
00:42:04.500 --> 00:42:06.450
OVERLAPPING MALE VOICES

597
00:42:06.500 --> 00:42:08.450
FOOTBALL MATCH ON TV

598
00:42:08.500 --> 00:42:10.500
MEN CHEER

599
00:42:12.500 --> 00:42:14.450
Yes!

600
00:42:14.500 --> 00:42:16.500
OVERLAPPING CHATTER

601
00:42:18.500 --> 00:42:20.500
Who's playing?

602
00:42:22.500 --> 00:42:24.500
Liverpool.

603
00:42:25.500 --> 00:42:27.440
It's not my team.

604
00:42:31.500 --> 00:42:32.770
Wait!

605
00:42:41.500 --> 00:42:43.900
Officer requesting backup!

606
00:42:45.500 --> 00:42:47.450
Just slow down!

607
00:42:47.500 --> 00:42:52.450
I just want to talk to
you! Wait! Slow down!

608
00:42:52.500 --> 00:42:54.450
I just want to talk to you!

609
00:42:54.500 --> 00:42:56.570
Why are you running?

610
00:43:00.500 --> 00:43:01.970
Get down!

611
00:43:02.500 --> 00:43:04.450
No! No!

612
00:43:04.500 --> 00:43:06.450
HEAVY BLOWS AND GRUNTING

613
00:43:06.500 --> 00:43:09.450
No! No!

614
00:43:09.500 --> 00:43:10.840
Aaagh!

615
00:43:13.500 --> 00:43:17.450
There was a playground near
my grandmother's house.

616
00:43:17.500 --> 00:43:20.500
No children. Not for miles.

617
00:43:21.500 --> 00:43:24.450
I used to think it was just for me.

618
00:43:24.500 --> 00:43:28.500
And I would see this old man
looking down at me from his flat.

619
00:43:30.500 --> 00:43:34.100
And he would wave at me
and I would wave back.

620
00:43:34.500 --> 00:43:38.450
So one day. I said to myself.
I'll go and knock on his door.

621
00:43:38.500 --> 00:43:40.500
I'll speak to him.

622
00:43:42.500 --> 00:43:44.840
I was a very nervous boy.

623
00:43:45.500 --> 00:43:51.500
But still I walked over to his block
of flats and knocked on the door.

624
00:43:53.500 --> 00:43:55.040
No-one in.

625
00:43:56.500 --> 00:44:00.500
I walked back home
across the playground...

626
00:44:03.500 --> 00:44:05.840
.. and there I saw him...

627
00:44:06.500 --> 00:44:08.640
.. lying in the snow.

628
00:44:13.500 --> 00:44:15.450
I didn't know what had happened. but...

629
00:44:15.500 --> 00:44:17.500
he was dead.

630
00:44:19.500 --> 00:44:21.570
And I ran so fast...

631
00:44:23.500 --> 00:44:25.450
.. to Mr Alghren's house.

632
00:44:25.500 --> 00:44:27.450
That's what everyone did.

633
00:44:27.500 --> 00:44:28.450
And he said...

634
00:44:28.500 --> 00:44:32.450
HE SPEAKS IN SWEDISH

635
00:44:32.500 --> 00:44:35.500
"I'm a policeman. you're all right now."

636
00:44:36.500 --> 00:44:38.570
And he took me home.

637
00:44:39.500 --> 00:44:42.500
But what I could see that he could not...

638
00:44:44.500 --> 00:44:47.500
.. the old man came home with me.

639
00:44:49.500 --> 00:44:51.500
And stayed.

640
00:44:54.500 --> 00:44:56.500
And talked to me.

641
00:44:58.500 --> 00:45:01.040
And I wasn't alone any more.

642
00:45:05.500 --> 00:45:07.700
Do you blame yourself?

643
00:45:08.500 --> 00:45:09.640
No.

644
00:45:10.500 --> 00:45:12.450
He was old. It was cold.

645
00:45:12.500 --> 00:45:14.100
For Stevie?

646
00:45:20.500 --> 00:45:22.570
It's understandable.

647
00:45:26.500 --> 00:45:29.450
Some people never encounter
death their entire lives.

648
00:45:29.500 --> 00:45:31.500
And you...

649
00:45:33.500 --> 00:45:35.450
.. you live with it...

650
00:45:35.500 --> 00:45:37.500
every day.

651
00:45:46.500 --> 00:45:49.500
MOBILE PHONE VIBRATES

652
00:45:55.500 --> 00:45:58.450
Hello.

653
00:45:58.500 --> 00:46:00.100
SIREN WAILS

654
00:46:14.500 --> 00:46:17.450
Christ! You idiot!

655
00:46:17.500 --> 00:46:18.450
Oh...

656
00:46:18.500 --> 00:46:21.450
- Shh. shh.
- Sorry. sorry. Are you all right?

657
00:46:21.500 --> 00:46:24.450
- Yeah. yeah. I'm fine. I'm fine.
- Oh. God. babe...

658
00:46:24.500 --> 00:46:26.040
This is...

659
00:46:27.450 --> 00:46:28.450
This is your fault.

660
00:46:28.500 --> 00:46:31.450
Do you know I cooked lamb
for you both tonight?

661
00:46:31.500 --> 00:46:33.450
- Marianne.
- Only he didn't ask you. did he?

662
00:46:33.500 --> 00:46:36.450
Cos that's not what you do. is
it? You don't actually talk.

663
00:46:36.500 --> 00:46:37.450
actually get to know one another.

664
00:46:37.500 --> 00:46:39.450
The only way I can do this.

665
00:46:39.500 --> 00:46:42.450
the only way that I can wait for
him to come home late at night

666
00:46:42.500 --> 00:46:44.450
is if I know you've got his back.

667
00:46:44.500 --> 00:46:46.450
You're his partner! That's
what you're meant to be.

668
00:46:46.500 --> 00:46:49.450
- Can we just go home?
- No. He works every hour God sends for you.

669
00:46:49.500 --> 00:46:50.450
to impress you.

670
00:46:50.500 --> 00:46:54.450
He's bringing papers home. falling
asleep in his dinner. For you!

671
00:46:54.500 --> 00:46:56.450
And you barely even talk to him.

672
00:46:56.500 --> 00:46:59.450
You barely even see him. Well. I see him.

673
00:46:59.500 --> 00:47:02.450
Because he's my partner.

674
00:47:02.500 --> 00:47:04.450
And I'm married to him too.

675
00:47:04.500 --> 00:47:07.500
So I need you... I need you to...

676
00:47:09.500 --> 00:47:11.450
Because...

677
00:47:11.500 --> 00:47:14.500
he is very precious... to me.

678
00:47:15.500 --> 00:47:17.500
He's important.

679
00:47:18.450 --> 00:47:19.450
All right?

680
00:47:19.500 --> 00:47:22.500
SOBBING BREATHS

681
00:47:25.500 --> 00:47:28.040
So come to dinner NEXT week.

682
00:47:28.500 --> 00:47:30.450
Nice to meet you.

683
00:47:30.500 --> 00:47:31.970
Come on.

684
00:47:33.500 --> 00:47:35.500
Oh. look at this.

685
00:47:38.500 --> 00:47:40.450
It's the same guy.

686
00:47:40.500 --> 00:47:43.500
THEY WHISPER TOGETHER

687
00:48:02.500 --> 00:48:03.700
Six.

688
00:48:05.500 --> 00:48:07.450
DOOR SLAMS

689
00:48:07.500 --> 00:48:10.500
- DOOR BANGS OPEN
- Get up.

690
00:48:12.500 --> 00:48:14.500
HE SPEAKS ROMANIAN

691
00:48:15.500 --> 00:48:17.900
He'll need an interpreter.

692
00:48:31.500 --> 00:48:36.450
Found wrapped in a shirt.
behind a hostel radiator.

693
00:48:36.500 --> 00:48:37.450
What's his name?

694
00:48:37.500 --> 00:48:42.450
Fedor Postan. 34 years
old. Moldovan. Unemployed.

695
00:48:42.500 --> 00:48:46.450
Overstayed his visa in March. May
have known Haider from the hostel.

696
00:48:46.500 --> 00:48:48.450
Any previous record?

697
00:48:48.500 --> 00:48:50.450
Where shall I begin?

698
00:48:50.500 --> 00:48:52.450
I'm Detective Chief
Inspector Chrissie Read

699
00:48:52.500 --> 00:48:56.450
- and this is my colleague. DI River.
- INTERPRETER TRANSLATES

700
00:48:56.500 --> 00:48:58.450
You will be charged with the
violent attack on my colleague.

701
00:48:58.500 --> 00:49:00.450
Detective Sergeant King. last night.

702
00:49:00.500 --> 00:49:06.450
- We also want to talk to you about the murder
of Haider Jamal Abdi. - TRANSLATION CONTINUES

703
00:49:06.500 --> 00:49:07.450
You do not have to say anything.

704
00:49:07.500 --> 00:49:09.450
but it may harm your defence
if you do not mention

705
00:49:09.500 --> 00:49:13.450
- when questioned something which you
later rely on in court... - Excuse me.

706
00:49:13.500 --> 00:49:16.500
Could you please go slower? Thank you.

707
00:49:19.500 --> 00:49:23.450
Anything you do say may
be given in evidence.

708
00:49:23.500 --> 00:49:26.450
SHE TRANSLATES

709
00:49:26.500 --> 00:49:27.450
Do you recognise this?

710
00:49:27.500 --> 00:49:29.500
SHE TRANSLATES

711
00:49:38.500 --> 00:49:40.450
HE WHISPERS

712
00:49:40.500 --> 00:49:42.500
No comment.

713
00:49:44.500 --> 00:49:47.450
You have been caught on camera
mopping a floor in the library

714
00:49:47.500 --> 00:49:50.450
where Mr Jamal Abdi was murdered.

715
00:49:50.500 --> 00:49:52.450
Yet the cleaning company has
no record of your employment.

716
00:49:52.500 --> 00:49:54.500
SHE INTERPRETS

717
00:50:03.500 --> 00:50:05.100
No comment.

718
00:50:07.500 --> 00:50:10.100
Your prints are on this knife.

719
00:50:11.500 --> 00:50:13.450
We will link you to this murder.

720
00:50:13.500 --> 00:50:16.100
So maybe you want to rethink.

721
00:50:16.500 --> 00:50:20.450
I'm offering you the chance to
help us and do yourself a favour.

722
00:50:20.500 --> 00:50:23.450
Give me a motive. because we have
the weapon. So start talking.

723
00:50:23.500 --> 00:50:26.500
SHE INTERPRETS

724
00:50:32.500 --> 00:50:34.450
HE SPEAKS ROMANIAN

725
00:50:34.500 --> 00:50:36.450
- I want to give a statement.
- Good.

726
00:50:36.500 --> 00:50:38.450
SHE INTERPRETS

727
00:50:38.500 --> 00:50:39.450
HE SPEAKS ROMANIAN

728
00:50:39.500 --> 00:50:41.500
I get a text.

729
00:50:43.500 --> 00:50:45.450
Someone leaves money for me to pick up.

730
00:50:45.500 --> 00:50:46.450
Where?

731
00:50:46.500 --> 00:50:48.450
- SHE INTERPRETS
- HE REPLIES

732
00:50:48.500 --> 00:50:50.450
The carwash in Dalston Lane.

733
00:50:50.500 --> 00:50:52.450
HE SPEAKS ROMANIAN

734
00:50:52.500 --> 00:50:54.450
I get a locker number and a key.

735
00:50:54.500 --> 00:50:57.450
HE SPEAKS ROMANIAN

736
00:50:57.500 --> 00:51:01.450
I was meant to pick up a second
instalment after the job was done.

737
00:51:01.500 --> 00:51:03.450
So you haven't picked it up yet?

738
00:51:03.500 --> 00:51:06.450
DCI Read is leaving the interview room.

739
00:51:06.500 --> 00:51:09.100
- SHE INTERPRETS
- DOOR SHUTS

740
00:51:11.500 --> 00:51:14.450
- Chrissie. - You get a
confession out of him and fast.

741
00:51:14.500 --> 00:51:17.600
- Are these his things?
- Yes. ma'am.

742
00:51:18.500 --> 00:51:21.450
Ah. locker 19.

743
00:51:21.500 --> 00:51:24.500
- I work with Tom.
- I know you do.

744
00:51:26.500 --> 00:51:29.100
You need to look at this list.

745
00:51:33.500 --> 00:51:37.450
This is Mrs Akentola's entire client list.

746
00:51:37.500 --> 00:51:42.450
Nothing left out. I don't think
Fedor even knew the man he killed.

747
00:51:42.500 --> 00:51:45.450
But these people are broke and will
do anything for a few hundred pounds

748
00:51:45.500 --> 00:51:47.450
and a promise of a visa.

749
00:51:47.500 --> 00:51:49.450
I can get others.

750
00:51:49.500 --> 00:51:52.450
One or two lawyers who I suspect
are doing exactly the same --

751
00:51:52.500 --> 00:51:56.450
ensuring clients' applications go
through. Paying judges when needed.

752
00:51:56.500 --> 00:52:00.500
to overlook discrepancies and
approve their right to stay here.

753
00:52:01.500 --> 00:52:03.500
Which judges?

754
00:52:04.500 --> 00:52:06.450
Which judges?!

755
00:52:06.500 --> 00:52:08.450
My client is waiting here! How
long are you going to hold him?

756
00:52:08.500 --> 00:52:10.500
We're charging him.

757
00:52:11.500 --> 00:52:13.040
Thank you.

758
00:52:17.500 --> 00:52:20.240
- Chrissie.
- Not yet. Not yet.

759
00:52:21.500 --> 00:52:24.700
Find out if there's a camera on locker 19.

760
00:52:48.500 --> 00:52:50.450
Couple of thousand.

761
00:52:50.500 --> 00:52:52.970
Is that the going rate now?

762
00:52:54.500 --> 00:52:58.450
Police. We need to pull up
some CCTV footage. please.

763
00:52:58.500 --> 00:53:00.040
Thank you.

764
00:53:07.500 --> 00:53:09.450
This is the last couple of days.

765
00:53:09.500 --> 00:53:11.100
It's there.

766
00:53:14.500 --> 00:53:16.450
This was yesterday?

767
00:53:16.500 --> 00:53:18.500
Yeah.

768
00:53:23.500 --> 00:53:25.500
Go back.

769
00:53:29.500 --> 00:53:30.840
There.

770
00:53:34.500 --> 00:53:36.500
Zoom in.

771
00:53:50.500 --> 00:53:52.840
I want all this footage.

772
00:53:53.500 --> 00:53:55.970
Get the whole team on this.

773
00:54:37.500 --> 00:54:40.450
We've bought a new sofa.

774
00:54:40.500 --> 00:54:43.040
Had the roof done in August.

775
00:54:45.500 --> 00:54:47.450
Came to about? £10.000.

776
00:54:47.500 --> 00:54:49.570
Paid for it in cash.

777
00:54:51.500 --> 00:54:53.500
He said it was...

778
00:54:57.500 --> 00:55:00.500
.. a back-dated... rebate.

779
00:55:02.500 --> 00:55:05.500
[SHE SNIFFLES] And there was more.

780
00:55:06.500 --> 00:55:09.500
It doesn't mean he was
involved in Stevie's death.

781
00:55:16.500 --> 00:55:20.450
Wait outside the house.
Just give me... ten minutes.

782
00:55:20.500 --> 00:55:22.450
Just... time to clear the kids.

783
00:55:22.500 --> 00:55:25.100
- Chrissie...
- Please don't.

784
00:56:05.500 --> 00:56:07.450
Hello. You want a drink?

785
00:56:07.500 --> 00:56:09.450
I sent the kids out for fish and chips.

786
00:56:09.500 --> 00:56:12.500
Genius. I've a tonne of
work to sign off on. so...

787
00:56:15.500 --> 00:56:17.450
What?

788
00:56:17.500 --> 00:56:18.970
DOORBELL

789
00:56:27.500 --> 00:56:29.500
TOM SIGHS

790
00:56:34.500 --> 00:56:36.450
Hello!

791
00:56:36.500 --> 00:56:39.040
We need to take you in. Tom.

792
00:56:39.500 --> 00:56:41.450
All right...

793
00:56:41.500 --> 00:56:42.450
Chrissie?

794
00:56:42.500 --> 00:56:45.370
We need to ask you some questions.

795
00:56:46.500 --> 00:56:48.450
Yeah. Chrissie....

796
00:56:48.500 --> 00:56:50.640
You are under arrest.

797
00:56:55.500 --> 00:56:59.450
- I just need to...
- No. Leave those.

798
00:56:59.500 --> 00:57:02.300
We need to go through everything.

799
00:57:03.500 --> 00:57:04.970
Chrissie.

800
00:57:07.500 --> 00:57:09.450
Chrissie!

801
00:57:09.500 --> 00:57:13.450
Tom Read. I am arresting you for
perverting the course of justice.

802
00:57:13.500 --> 00:57:16.450
You do not have to say anything.
but it may harm your defence

803
00:57:16.500 --> 00:57:18.450
if you do not mention

804
00:57:18.500 --> 00:57:21.450
when questioned something which
you later rely on in court.

805
00:57:21.500 --> 00:57:23.570
Excuse me. Chrissie?

806
00:57:24.500 --> 00:57:25.970
CHRISSIE!

807
00:57:26.500 --> 00:57:28.500
Come on. Tom.

808
00:57:59.500 --> 00:58:01.450
♪ Sunny

809
00:58:01.500 --> 00:58:06.450
♪ Yesterday my life was filled with rain

810
00:58:06.500 --> 00:58:08.500
♪ Sunny

811
00:58:09.500 --> 00:58:13.450
♪ You smiled at me and
really eased the pain

812
00:58:13.500 --> 00:58:18.450
♪ The dark days are done
and the bright days are here

813
00:58:18.500 --> 00:58:21.450
♪ My Sunny one shines so sincere

814
00:58:21.500 --> 00:58:26.500
♪ Sunny one. so true. I love you. ♪

815
00:58:29.500 --> 00:58:32.450
The Curious Incident Of The Dog
In The Night-time has transformed

816
00:58:32.500 --> 00:58:36.450
our understanding of a condition
that affects 1 in 100 children.

817
00:58:36.500 --> 00:58:38.450
The world is illogical.

818
00:58:38.500 --> 00:58:40.500
and that's a big problem
for people on the spectrum.
